-- title:
--   Level-M' laws along an Igusa branch at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$ and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Global level-$M'$ reduction data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$, so that $A$ has residue characteristic $q$. The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the subfield of `LaurentSeries (ResidueField A)` generated over `ResidueField A` by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'` — is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ (valuation subrings of that field containing the base field, proper, with principal ideals) which are rational, i.e. the map from `ResidueField A` to the residue field of $w$ is surjective, which satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which `w.evalAt (jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M')` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over `ResidueField A` with invariant $j$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion affine point. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, itself generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d$ of $M'$) with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, whose contraction to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$ and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with the scaling property, a place map preserving degrees, and the divisor push-forward compatibility. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies this reduction with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along `IsLocalRing.residue A`. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   **The local base and its uniformiser.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hπ`). Writing $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$, the hypotheses `hdvr` and `hunif` say that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Auxiliary level $\ell'$ and the function field $K_\ell$.** $\ell'$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell'$, $\ell' \ne q$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$. The hypothesis `hKℓ` fixes $K_\ell$ to be `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀` applied to `xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ')^2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M')`, that is, the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH (q * ℓ') M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K_\ell$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. The element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is non-zero and has Laurent series `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq` (`hjℓ`).
--
--   **The supersingular point $y$.** $y$ is an ideal of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥Kℓ jℓ`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ of elements integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; `hy` asserts that $y$ is maximal, `hϖy` that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $y$, and `hss` that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel exactly $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ (the distinguished element `jChartFin`) lies in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hover` ($y$ lies over $s$).** For every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers`, such that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the order of $g$ at $P$ is non-negative whenever the order of (the image of) `jq` at $P$ is, and such that the residue `R₀.residue g` lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: for every proof that `qExpand ↥k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb ↥k₀ g)` lies in $K_\ell$ and that the resulting element lies in the chart algebra, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals `s.evalAt (R₀.residue g)`, the difference between that chart-algebra element and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   **The Igusa coordinate.** `hjK` and `hjC` say that `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * ℓ')`, the $(q\ell')$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling of the $j$-expansion, lies in $K_\ell$ and that the resulting element lies in the chart algebra; $a_0 \in A_0$ is such that this element minus the image of $a_0$ lies in $y$ (`ha₀y`). The element $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`).
--
--   **The valuation ring $W_t$ centred at $y$.** $W_t$ is a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ such that, by `hR3d`, an element $b$ of the chart algebra lies in $y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $W_t$ and lies in the maximal ideal of $W_t$.
--
--   **The deck group and its fixed field.** $G$ is a subgroup of the $k_0$-automorphism group of $K_\ell$ such that (`hGatt`) every $\tau \in G$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ (q * ℓ') ξ (q * ℓ') ((q * ℓ')^2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M') γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` for some $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ belonging both to $\Gamma(q)$ and to $\Gamma_0(M')$; this predicate requires that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g$ having non-zero series over $\mathbb Q$, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the series of $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid[k]$`conjElemN (q*ℓ') γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid[k]$`conjElemN (q*ℓ') γ⁻¹`. The field $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`).
--
--   **The ends $\tilde O$ and $O$.** $\tilde O$ is a subring of $K_\ell$ containing the chart algebra (`hCO`) and contained in $W_t$ (`hOW`); $O$ is the subring of $K_0$ obtained as the contraction of $\tilde O$ along the inclusion of $K_0$ in $K_\ell$ (`hOdef`).
--
--   **The Igusa branch $W_x$.** $W_x$ is a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $\tilde O$ (`hOWx`) and the chart algebra (`hCWx`), whose contraction to $k_0$ is $A_0$: by `hVA`, an element of $k_0$ has image in $W_x$ exactly when it comes from $A_0$. By `hcentre`, any element $b$ of the chart algebra which lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ (whenever it lies in $W_x$) already lies in $y$, while by `hne` there is an element of the chart algebra lying in $y$ but not in the maximal ideal of $W_x$. Finally `hVj` asserts the residual transcendence of the Igusa coordinate: for every polynomial $p$ over $A_0$, if the value at `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * ℓ')` of the polynomial obtained from $p$ by coefficient extension to $k_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the order of $g$ at $P$ is non-negative whenever the order of `jq` at $P$ is, and for every proof that $g^\sharp :=$ `qExpand ↥k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb ↥k₀ g)` lies in $K_\ell$, the element $g^\sharp$ of $K_\ell$ lies in $K_0$, and as an element of $K_0$ it satisfies the following three assertions.
--
--   First, $g^\sharp$ lies in the contraction of $W_x$ to $K_0$.
--
--   Second, for any such membership, $g^\sharp$ lies in the maximal ideal of that contraction if and only if `R₀.residue g` is $0$ in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`.
--
--   Third, if `R₀.residue g` lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then $g^\sharp$ lies in $O$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose image in $K_0$ lies in $O$ and whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals `s.evalAt (R₀.residue g)`, the difference of $g^\sharp$ and $c$, taken in $O$, is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   This is the per-node step of the descent analysis of the special fibre of a model of the modular curve of level $M'$ at a supersingular point, in the Igusa-curve picture: it transfers the reduction laws for level-$M'$ modular functions from the chart algebra of the auxiliary rigid level $(q\ell')^2M'$ down to the fixed field $K_0$ of the deck group, along a branch $W_x$ through the point $y$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps) in the assembly of the node-by-node conclusion about traces.
